    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released **version 2 of the owner identity**, keeping each piece of logic in a small, single-responsibility unit.\n\n**New `model/IdentityVersion.java`** \u2014 the single source of truth for the release. It owns the version number (`NUMBER = 2`, used for both the response `apiVersion` and the audit `schemaVersion`) and the fixed `TAG = \"V2\"`, plus three tiny helpers: `mix(key)` (folds the tag into a hashed identifier's input), `regionCode(plain)` (tags the region embedded in the member id), and `plainRegion(code)` (strips the tag back off).\n\n**Identifiers rederived with the V2 tag** (every value changes, none collides with v1):\n- **memberId** \u2014 `MemberIdGenerator` now embeds `IdentityVersion.regionCode(\"NSW\")` \u2192 `\"V2NSW\u2026\"`. Because a v1 region never starts with `V2`, no v1 member id is ever reproduced.\n- **householdId** \u2014 `HouseholdIdGenerator` mixes the tag into the hashed `lastName|postcode` key.\n- **identityKey** \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` mixes the tag into its hash input (duplicate detection stays consistent since both sides compute it the same way).\n\n**Locality stays the plain region** \u2014 `Owner.getLocality()` reads the region back from the member id and strips the `V2` tag, so `locality` (`NSW`), `timezone`, and the owner segment's derived region are unaffected by the tag. Confirmed by the audit segment `STANDARD_METRO` (area METRO from plain `NSW`).\n\n**Response shape** \u2014 in `openapi.yml` I removed top-level `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId`, added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema, nested those three under an `identity` object, and added an integer `apiVersion`. `OwnerMapper` populates `apiVersion` (from `IdentityVersion.NUMBER`) and builds the nested `identity`.\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema v2** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` now stamps `schemaVersion: 2` and carries `ownerSegment`, recomputed from the owner's v2 identity. Verified in the emitted JSON: `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\u2026,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\u2026}`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.",
