    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:157-215`).\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (L157). Caller must have `OWNER_ADMIN` \u2192 else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, interface is `@Validated`). Runs on the *raw* submitted values, in field order:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (optional); `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - Any violation \u2192 400.\n\n## In the controller body (in order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** (L160-167) \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, return the previously created owner with **200 OK**; no new owner created.\n4. **Address normalization \u2014 SIDE EFFECT, mutates the DTO** (L168 \u2192 `resolveAddress`). Trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE), and resolves the flat `address` from the structured lines. *Note: this runs after Bean Validation, so validation saw the raw values.*\n5. **Manual missing-field check** (L169-172, `OwnerFieldsValidator`) \u2014 blank check on firstName, lastName, address (addressLine1 OR address), city, telephone \u2192 400.\n6. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping \u2014 SIDE EFFECT** (L174, MapStruct `ownerMapper.toOwner`); id and pets ignored.\n7. **Postcode-vs-city range check** (L175-177, `PostcodeValidator`) \u2192 400.\n8. **City capacity check \u2014 DB READ** (L178-180) \u2014 reject if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 409.\n9. **Future registration-date check** (L181-183) \u2192 400.\n10. **Daily registration limit \u2014 DB READ** (L184-187) \u2014 computes the effective (business-day-rolled) date and rejects if \u2265 100 owners registered that day \u2192 429.\n11. **Telephone normalization \u2014 SIDE EFFECT + validation** (L188) \u2014 canonical E.164; invalid \u2192 400.\n12. **Email normalization \u2014 SIDE EFFECT** (L189) \u2014 trim + lower-case (blank \u2192 null).\n13. **Disposable-email check** (L190-192) \u2014 blocks mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail \u2192 400.\n14. **Household id generation \u2014 SIDE EFFECT** (L193) \u2014 SHA-256-derived `householdId` from lastName + postcode.\n15. **Declared-membership flag \u2014 SIDE EFFECT** (L194-197) \u2014 set `declaredHouseholdMember` from the transient `sharesHousehold`.\n16. **Duplicate-identity check \u2014 DB READ, conditional** (L198-204) \u2014 skipped if the owner declared shared household; otherwise matches on telephone + identity key \u2192 409.\n\n## Persist \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner` (L205, `@Transactional`)\n\nBecause the owner is new, these run in order (each with DB reads), then the INSERT:\n\n17. **Generate `memberId`** \u2014 region + fiscal year + hash + Luhn check digit, de-duplicated against existing member ids (repeated DB reads).\n18. **Set `namesakeCount`** \u2014 DB read counting owners with same first+last name.\n19. **Set `householdSize`** \u2014 DB read of household members + 1.\n20. **Set `membershipLevelCap`** \u2014 one above the max membership level in the household (or null).\n21. **Detect possible duplicate** \u2014 skipped for declared household members; else scans owners for same postcode + Soundex-equal last name but different identity key. Sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n22. **`ownerRepository.save` \u2192 `em.persist`** (INSERT). During persist:\n    - **`@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate`** \u2014 defaults null \u2192 today and rolls weekends/holidays forward; this is the stored value.\n    - **Entity-level Bean Validation** on `Owner`/`Person`: `@NotEmpty` on firstName, lastName, address, city; telephone `@NotEmpty` + E.164 `@Pattern` (validates the *normalized* value).\n    - `pets` cascade is `ALL` but empty on create \u2192 no cascade inserts.\n\n## After save \u2014 post-persist side-effects (in order)\n\n23. **Audit** (L206, `OwnerAuditor.ownerCreated`) \u2014 logs to the `AUDIT` logger, increments a sequence, emits an `OwnerCreatedEvent` as JSON.\n24. **Welcome notification** (L207, `WelcomeNotifier.welcome`) \u2014 logs \"welcome notification enqueued\" to the `NOTIFY` logger (log only; no real email).\n25. **Remember idempotency key** (L208-210) \u2014 `putIfAbsent(key, ownerId)` in the in-memory store.\n26. **Map to response + advisory warnings** (L211, `toOwnerDtoWithWarnings`) \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (adds selfLink, displayName, telephoneDisplay, apiVersion, nested identity) and, via additional DB reads, stamps advisory flags: bulk-signup warning (>80/day), capacity warning (city in [40,50)), risk flag (possible duplicate, disposable-adjacent email, or city \u2265 40).\n27. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\nA key ordering nuance worth flagging: DTO-level pattern/size validation (step 2) runs against **raw** input, while normalization of address, telephone, and email happens *afterward* (steps 4, 11, 12) \u2014 so the entity's E.164 telephone `@Pattern` (step 22) is the one validating the normalized phone value, not the DTO constraint."
